[   97.0s] no cited statement shows that the generators of the parabolic at Integral lattice of rank 2 and signature (0, 0) generate the setwise stabilizer: Dutour Sikirić--Hulek Theorem 4.9 (arXiv:2302.01679v2, printed p. 22) solves the block equations and their Alg 1 (same paper, section 'Integral group algorithms') computes the integral points of a rational group, but neither names a generating set of the parabolic. The plane action is decided: levi_plane_action_index() gives the index of the returned plane actions in GL_2(ZZ) by the Gamma(2) certificate (1 at Sterk's P_2 of T_En, where det J = 4 makes J a scalar and imposes no congruence). The quotient factor is decided: levi_quotient_image_index() gives [10321920 : 10321920] = 1 for the image H_0 of the returned generators in O(I^perp/I), so the image of the whole setwise stabilizer there is H_0, i.e. all of O(I^perp/I). Decided, and negative: the radical U_I is not generated. All 14 returned unipotent transvections lie in it (each fixes the plane pointwise and acts trivially on I^perp/I, measured), and 28 of the 122 generators of this family do; but U_I has rank 17 = 2 rank(I^perp/I) + 1 by the block form (unipotent_radical_rank()), of which 1 is fixed by the translation map (unipotent_translation_kernel_rank()) and 16 are translations, while the translations of the returned family have rank 12 and those of the 28 radical members of this family have rank 14. Both families therefore generate subgroups of infinite index, and unipotent_radical_index() returns aleph_0. A cited generation statement is missing for the same reason it was missing before: Scattone, Mem. Amer. Math. Soc. 374, section 3.7, Proposition 3.7.3, generates the radical by Eichler transvections only over two orthogonal hyperbolic planes, which T_En does not have.
